# Reassembling the active-dyadic finite product

At a fixed dyadic frequency, the `TT*` operator is the literal product
kernel on `R^d × Z_j`.  Its index set is already finite, but the canonical
gap level is only bounded on pairs of *active* indices.  This file first
replaces the unrestricted relation by the extensionally identical active
